meta { title = "Kalandra documentation", description = "Learn the language, look up its rules and build CPU and GPU programs.", order = 0, group = "Start here" }

Kalandra is a compiled language for CPU and GPU computing. A program is made of typed functions. You can run those functions on the CPU, start independent tasks, or place supported numerical work on a GPU. Memory is managed automatically; data transfers to and from a GPU are explicit.

h2 { "New to Kalandra?" }

Install the toolchain, run your first program, then follow the tutorial. You need basic programming experience, but no prior knowledge of Kalandra, GPU programming or its compiler.

list {
  link { url = "/docs/installation", "Installation — choose a package for your computer" },
