h2 { "A first program" }

codeblock { language = kalandra, """from "std/io" import println, IoError
from "std/fmt" import format

fn main() -> unit ! IoError:
  output: i64 = 6 * 7

  try println(format("{}", output))
  return ()
""" }

Save this as main.k. In a macOS or Linux terminal, check it, compile it, then run the executable:

codeblock { language = bash, """kalandra-check main.k
kalandra main.k -o program
./program
""" }

The executable displays 42, the result of main. On Windows, compile with -o program.exe and run ./program.exe. There is no interactive prompt or separate run command in this workflow.

Unless a page names companion files, each complete language example is a separate program: replace main.k rather than appending examples together. Command blocks contain commands to enter, without shell prompts. GPU examples need a backend-enabled package and the commands in the GPU guide.

h2 { "Contribute" }

The contributor guide explains the source layout, builds, tests and documentation workflow. Use GitHub for proposals, implementation discussions and project planning.

